--TEST--
`new class { … }` is refused at the keyword — a class declaration is not an expression
--FILE--
<?nvs
// An anonymous class is a nested declaration in expression position, with no
// name for the static class table to hold; `nvs_ir` has nothing to lower it
// under, which is why the refusal is the parser's rather than a later phase's.
// The value is discarded here so the one error is the refusal itself: a
// binding would carry a second one about the type the expression has instead.
interface Greeter {
    public function greet(): string;
}

new class implements Greeter {
    public function greet(): string {
        return "hello";
    }
};

// covers: lang:classes/what-a-class-cannot-declare
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0244]: a class declaration is not an expression
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
